#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Thesaurus Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Thesaurus</guilabel> tab offers a small thesaurus, built from "
"a subset of <link linkend=\"frontend\">&wordnet;</link>. The results are "
"listed in three categories: <guilabel>Synonyms</guilabel>, <guilabel>More "
"General Words</guilabel> (hypernyms), <guilabel>More Specific Words</"
"guilabel> (hyponyms). Synonyms are words with a very similar meaning. They "
"do not necessarily apply to all senses of each word, so you cannot always "
"replace a word with any synonym."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can double click on a word to search for its synonyms &etc;. You can "
"also type a word directly into the <guilabel>Search for:</guilabel> box at "
"the top and press <keycap>Return</keycap>. The word which is currently "
"visible in the <guilabel>Replace with:</guilabel> box at the bottom is the "
"one that will be used if you click on <guibutton>Replace</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kthesaurus; can be used as a standalone application, but it can also be "
"used from other applications (like &kword;, typically by right clicking on a "
"word and selecting <guilabel>Show related words</guilabel>). The "
"<guibutton>Replace with:</guibutton> button will only be visible if "
"&kthesaurus; is called from another application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We have to keep the data file small so that it can be included in &koffice; "
"&mdash; this introduces several limitations (compared to &wordnet;):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only exact matches are found, &eg; if you search for a plural form nothing "
"will be found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Many not so common words have been removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It doesn't distinguish between parts of speech, &eg; verbs and nouns are "
"mixed up in the lists of words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "It won't separate the different meanings words can have."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adjectives don't really have a <quote>more general</quote> / <quote>more "
"specific</quote> meaning, so one word may appear in more than one list at "
"the same time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the other hand, a few words have been added (function words like "
"<quote>if</quote> and very few words specific to &kde;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please do <emphasis>not</emphasis> report bugs in the thesaurus to the "
"&wordnet; project, but to &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using languages besides English"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, only the English language is supported in &kthesaurus;. You can "
"check out <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/addons/#thesauri\">the "
"&koffice; download page</ulink> to see which other languages are available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &wordnet; tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>&wordnet;</guilabel> tab provides a user interface to a local "
"installation of <ulink url=\"http://wordnet.princeton.edu/\">&wordnet;</"
"ulink>. &wordnet; is <quote>an online lexical reference system whose design "
"is inspired by current psycholinguistic theories of human lexical memory.</"
"quote> The &kthesaurus; user interface offers nearly all options which are "
"available on the command line. It calls the <command>wn</command> binary, "
"which has to be in your <envar>PATH</envar>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To learn more about &wordnet;, please see the &wordnet; <command>man</"
"command> pages or have a look at the <ulink url=\"http://wordnet.princeton."
"edu/\">&wordnet; homepage</ulink>."
msgstr ""

